Reference verification (pst-t0ob3.1 REV 3b and REV 3c, mayor 2026-10-11):
Compare facet count, bbox (1e-6 mm), signed volume (1e-6 relative), and
canonical triangle vertices (exact or within 1e-6 mm). REV 3c also accepts
unmatched triangles when all their vertices lie within 1e-4 mm of vertices
in the other mesh AND they form coplanar quads with the same vertex set
split on alternate diagonals. All ten renders PASS under these rules.
Committed meshes are the mayor baselines copied verbatim; SHA256SUMS records
those baseline bytes. Both baseline and independent worker hashes follow.

From the repository root, set OPENSCADPATH to the parent of the pinned
BOSL2 checkout. Commands below independently render to the named mesh path;
replace the output with the verified mayor baseline before committing.

